#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Synthetic JevBench-shaped decision rows with labels derived by rule (no model anywhere).

Families (all generated by default; `--families a,b` to restrict):
  long_policy       8-15k-char policy packs (procurement approval, returns desk, insurance sublimit, licence
                    true-up, payment relief, incident severity): definitions, amendments with effective dates,
                    annexes, worked examples, FAQ, change log, then a case file with a tempting wrong draft.
  temporal_numeric  warranty end dates (month-end rule, time zones), budget alerts (running sums, credits, tax
                    excluded), dose intervals across zones, rest violations across DST, weekly rota compliance,
                    pro-rata refunds (leap years, fee windows), loan interest (act/360, business-day resets),
                    card declines (running limits, holds, fees), FX lodging (rate-date rule, nightly caps), and
                    compact {event, rules} JSON bands (elapsed windows, TiB vs GB, day proration, percentages).
  multi_hop         on-call routing chains (process -> service -> team -> merge -> rotation -> zone -> override),
                    bursary assessments (status -> household -> countable income -> table -> cap), and JSON
                    registry chains with footnotes, amendments, archive distractors and a strict boundary.
  routing_tradeoff  ranked precedence rules whose definitions defeat surface cues, handler selection, dispatch
                    tradeoffs under ordered rules, and control checklists (yes/no).
  trap_adversarial  trusted-vs-claimed evidence: access decisions, priority from telemetry, ticket disposition,
                    condition established by trusted facts, instant-refund eligibility.
  noul_yesno        yes/no with true/false criteria: policy permitted (unproved = unmet), facts strictly stated
                    (negations, plans, hypotheticals), adequacy of a response to explicit constraints.
  score_levels      ordered level indices: incident impact (highest fully supported), counts of rule breaches,
                    shortfall bands with inclusive boundaries.
  judge_verify      request/response pairs; the response may hide an arithmetic slip, wrong rounding, unit
                    factor error, miscounted business days, or an unmet presentation constraint (true/false).
  probability_freq  most likely outcome from a frequency table after conditioning or filtering rows.

Conventions match how JevBench items reach our server: choice = snake_case option keys with descriptions;
noul = criteria keyed "true"/"false" (expected is "true"/"false"; the harness maps true->yes); score = keys
"0".."k" in level order (expected is the level index as a string).

Every label is computed from the latent facts that generated the state. Entities, wording and numbers are
generated here; nothing is copied from the benchmark items or the frozen eval sets, and `--check` asserts
zero exact or 120-character-prefix overlap of states, instructions and option descriptions with them.

usage:
  synth_jevbench.py OUT_DIR [--n 500] [--seed 7] [--families long_policy,temporal_numeric,...]
  synth_jevbench.py OUT_DIR --check          # overlap check + per-family label balance of rows in OUT_DIR
writes OUT_DIR/train.jsonl and OUT_DIR/dev.jsonl (10% of groups) in the training row format
{id, group, source, state, instructions, criteria, expected, upstream_split}, plus summary.json.
"""
